id: E545
draft: true
title: Audit release versus tag source scope before restoring a conditionally registered CMake suite
trigger_tool: cmake|ctest|conan
phase: source|testing
error_signature: WITH_UNIT_TESTS.*ON|if\(EXISTS.*test|100% tests passed.*out of 1
severity: 2
category: cmake, build-system, detection
match_keywords: conditional test subdirectory, EXISTS, release archive, Git tag, tests enabled, silent coverage contraction, test inventory
root_cause: CMake can enable tests but conditionally omit a development suite when its source directory is absent. A release archive and a same-version Git tag can therefore register different denominators while both configuration and CTest exit successfully; the tests-on option is not evidence of full upstream coverage. An immutable official tag URL can end in a commit SHA while delivering tar.gz bytes. Conan uses the downloaded filename to choose archive handling, so declare the real filename/container without changing the URL or SHA256.
affected_scope: C/C++ projects whose complete tag contains development tests conditionally added through directory existence checks, while release packaging omits that directory.
verification_cmd: Bind the immutable official tag tree and archive hash, inspect the conditional add_subdirectory and named case list, then run verbose CTest and compare both executable and logical-case denominators.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: source-bound-conditional-suite-inventory
rec_description: Inventory the authoritative upstream tag before accepting the release archive's denominator. If an eligible development suite is silently absent, obtain a complete immutable official source archive, verify its tree/blob closure, keep the upstream CMake entry enabled, and require all registered programs and named development cases to pass. Guard the recipe against the missing directory; report consumer assertions separately. An immutable official tag URL can end in a commit SHA while delivering tar.gz bytes. Conan uses the downloaded filename to choose archive handling, so declare the real filename/container without changing the URL or SHA256.
rec_command: cmake -S complete-official-source -B build -DWITH_UNIT_TESTS=ON; cmake --build build --parallel 2; ctest --test-dir build --verbose --output-on-failure
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: preserve-incomplete-state
fallback_description: If the complete official input cannot be verified or any eligible test fails, preserve the real partial/FAIL result and do not substitute release-only or consumer coverage.
fallback_auto_fix: false
forbid_1_pattern: WITH_UNIT_TESTS.*ON.*full.coverage|release.*1/1.*all.upstream
forbid_1_reason: Successful testing only proves the actual registered source-dependent subset, not the omitted suite.
forbid_1_consequence: Hidden upstream under-reporting despite a green build.
safety_boundary: Do not infer tests from names alone, accept partial archives, fetch floating source, modify expected outputs, exclude failing registered cases, or reinterpret a consumed failed transaction as PASS. Complete-tag source must also remain independently buildable; this pattern is not a general replacement of release archives by Git snapshots.
similar_to: DRAFT-libfsntfs-release-archive-closure, E2185-draft-2301_80739235, DRAFT-geographiclib-2.7-data-gated-ctest-recovery, DRAFT-uvg266-0.8.1-greatest-test-submodule-multi-source
novelty_boundary: Silent EXISTS registration is already known from geographiclib data gates and uvg266 missing test-framework submodules; do not re-claim that generic rule. The new increment is diagnosing same-project test SOURCE omitted only by release packaging: data injection, test_requires, and submodule fetching cannot restore it. Select the complete immutable SAME upstream tag only when it independently builds and every official Git blob matches; reject missing development inventory, and reconcile each registered program's internal logical cases (including rendering fixtures) rather than mixing program and case units. libfsntfs addresses generated-file/bundled-source closure, E2185 unregistered utility self-checks; neither proves this release-versus-tag conditional suite recovery boundary.
verification_evidence: libxmp 4.7.3 release archive registers one CTest; complete commit 1e0812137e4f9e15cc026c0c75af82d71d3cb5ad contains test-dev with1013 named cases and registers two CTest programs. Release test/test.c additionally has3 run_test renders: test.it, test.itz, test.xm, giving1016 logical cases, not1014. Full archive SHA256 f2ee83c3ec146d5024bcba2a094ba9cf48eebbf9518bca02cf2e7cb139889a43 has all3277 official Git blobs verified. Native r5 and official finish W3 r1 independently passed; W3 log SHA256 85ae574b3461e95b2b4d176d6a2d7e94633e7af90c3d0164b87aa36096fa9c64, exact1013 names plus3 original rendering MD5 passes and installed consumer131 assertions. Aggregate finish RC1 and legacy G1 FAIL preserved; r4 redundant Make failure remains FAIL. No recipe test source or expected output changed.
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/E545-draft-XM11.md
last_updated: 2026-10-13
source_event: libxmp complete-tag native r5 PASS (1013/1013 development cases, 2/2 CTest programs, consumer 131 assertions); log SHA256 93c0d1d05074d7f5674b5cb00cc898b7a7d9ecd515e3e32d3c7f4b20b373259f 2026-10-13 current CI repair; libxmp-ci-repair-w3-20261013-r1, official CI log SHA256 fea19818afc60855ef0511a942a013ecef1af9e89026f36b76f891d7654644b0; Do not re-claim generic complete-tag coverage. The new boundary is that a local archive override ending in tar.gz can mask a filename-based unpack failure on the extensionless official CI URL; independently check both source() argument routing and the pinned container identity before claiming reproducibility.
authors: 2501_91199785
contributor_id: XM11
